{
  "assessment": "Source closure is rejected for the family as written. The closed-form Oracle itself is numerically source-faithful: on 10,001 St values over [0.01,300], each materialized AST branch agreed with the independently evaluated source-derived fit to at most 8.89e-16; all diagnostic and hidden predictions agreed exactly at stored precision, both branches were separated at every listed prediction, the public/private conditions were properly partitioned, and the readout correctly represents a deterministic fit-derived normalized central value rather than raw measurements. However, relationship_targets[0] states for both branches that r increases with St while its bound directions say decreasing. Since alpha_mu is below alpha_phi=0.1 in both source regimes, K_mu(St)=0.065(1+alpha_mu St)/(1+0.1 St), hence r(St), decreases throughout the declared interval and approaches its plateau from above. That false process target prevents an objectively correct family verdict.",
  "decision": "source_closure_rejected",
  "family": "viscous_inertial_rheology",
  "issues": [
    {
      "code": "family.relationship_shape_contradiction",
      "detail": "review_material.relationship_targets[0].historical_shape and .counterfactual_shape both state that r increases with St, contradicting the correctly bound decreasing directions, the materialized AST, every ordered prediction sequence, and the source-derived fit. For alpha_mu=0.029 or 0.00875, both below alpha_phi=0.1, dr/dSt is strictly negative on St in [0.01,300]. Revise both shape strings to say that r decreases with St and approaches a finite plateau from above.",
      "line_ranges": [
        {
          "line_start": 177,
          "line_end": 177
        },
        {
          "line_start": 246,
          "line_end": 252
        },
        {
